title The minutes a seed publish spent starting grep
prompt Autonomous lap. Reds first, Lindy first, card's agent-doable queue.
rota lap 5209, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; the concrete fact at the door was a stopwatch, and it pointed away from the cure REDS %642 had booked for nine days
think My lane's own asks want Keaton's word, so I took the card's first agent-doable item under claim-as-override: %642, the seed scrub cache.
think Before building the booked cure I measured the thing it is named for. The timing paper prices the projection's three per-file greps at 215 of its 365 seconds; over a 500-path sample of the same set a per-file grep loop runs 6,624 ms where one grep over the same files runs 186 ms.
think So the cost was starting grep rather than reading bytes, and the repair is batching rather than caching -- no new state, no staleness window, no key, no version.
think Claimed it on construction/fleet-claims.kyri and pushed the claim before touching a file, since the row was a booked red every ship reads.
think Kept the elder candidate walk byte for byte rather than widening it, because one candidate path carries a space and the manifest's own sub_exclude for it is truncated by awk field 2 -- two faults that cancel, booked as %804.
think Proved parity on the real field three ways rather than by a diff exit code: diff -r prints 26 lines and every one is diff declining a dangling symlink into the withheld linengrow.
obs sow_reach_inputs reddened on the first draft and was right to: its control plants a sed that exits 9, and my directory pass piped through sed, so a broken sed failed where a directory would have been made rather than where the scrub is. awk writes the prefix now.
obs The roster's own note explained the sow guard's slow clock by calling its cost inherent -- real work rather than a fork loop. Most of it was a fork loop; the note carries the correction and the row keeps its cadence tier on its other reason.
obs plant_liveness caught a DEAD PLANT in my own new control: the ceiling-lift mutation rewrote SOW_MAX_CANDIDATES to the value it already carried, so that phase tested the unmutated file and proved only what the first leg proved. It reads 64 now, and the guard is green at plants_dead=0.
obs Reds first reached my own lane's elder file: instrument_refusal named tools/fixtures/b/kyri_resins_landed_scan.sh twice, where two git log walks piped straight into awk with 2>/dev/null and || true, so a git that could not run read as a room with no history. Each walk is read into a file first now and git's own status is checked; swallowed_instrument_passes fell 2 to 0 and the remaining 2 are a peer's fallback sites.
obs The hot endurance run reads tree_moved=yes, and the three moved paths are mine: a peer's build lock vanished, and I repaired kyri_resins_landed_scan.sh and sow_project.sh while the pass ran. Every guard those two can move was re-run green by hand afterward.
obs My baseline projection reddened sow_allow_reach on the cold endurance run by clearing seed/.sow-projection.log beside a roster pass. REDS %193's own class, met from the other side; green again after.
